      "lineNbr": 1774,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-23T20:55:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That seems reasonable.  We could just have it named `flushPendingWork(DrawContext*)` and if the DC is null, then we add `drawTask` to the root task list.\n\nI think we also want to be clear about the assignment to `fLastTask` being skipped if we provide a non-null DrawContext. If we don\u0027t assign `fLastTask`, then the surfaces created for CopyAsDraw will not go through the pending-read ref counting that lets us reuse short-lived textures. Lets work through what that looks like in the CopyAsDraw and the GenerateMipmaps case to make sure we aren\u0027t regressing the texture reuse.\n\nAlthough in the future, I think there\u0027s potential to simplify this where a Surface could be created with a parent DrawContext instead of a Recorder.  In that case even if it were a \"scratch\" surface, we\u0027d go through the code flow in notifyInUse() that flushes the task to its \"root\" and then we would probably be able to get rid of all internal explicit flushes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1774,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1774,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "90d6c136819eb8116b51debfe303f48bf84ce771",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
